    title: "National Pension in Chiyoda", summary: "Chiyoda separates Category I changes, contribution relief, and student applications by filing counter.",
    applicability: "Use Chiyoda's procedures if Chiyoda is your responsible municipality and your coverage category calls for a municipal National Pension filing.", responsibleBody: "Chiyoda City", receivingOffice: "National Pension Section at Chiyoda City Office or a branch office for eligible filings; contribution exemption and payment postponement go to the main section",
    actions: [
      { title: "Bring evidence for the coverage change", description: "After leaving an employer pension plan, Chiyoda asks for your Basic Pension Number Notice or pension book and a document issued by the employer, Japan Pension Service, or Hello Work that shows the employer and actual retirement date, bears the required stamp, and is not based on a planned future date. After leaving a spouse's dependent coverage, bring the pension-number record and proof of the date that dependent status ended. These notifications can go to the ward's National Pension Section or a branch office. If you become a dependent spouse instead, the ward directs the notification through your spouse's employer. The page does not specify documents for a first enrollment after arrival from abroad, so check that case with the National Pension Section." },
      { title: "Use the correct relief counter or electronic procedure", description: "Chiyoda handles contribution exemption and payment-postponement applications at the main National Pension Section, not a branch office; an unemployment-based application needs additional separation evidence. Student Special Payment applications can go to the main section or a branch office with an original enrollment certificate or a copy of both sides of the student ID. The ward also lists electronic applications for Category I acquisition or change, relief, and student postponement; check the linked Japan Pension Service instructions for the appropriate online form." },
    ],
    sourceIds: ["chiyoda-national-pension-procedures"], sourceFormatNote: "Chiyoda's current National Pension procedure page is in Japanese. This English summary is Nihonest guidance, not an official translation.",
