    actions: [
      { title: "Ask which records apply after an overseas move", description: "Chuo lists arrival from abroad among events needing a National Pension notification after resident registration. Its page directs residents to ask the Pension Section which documents to bring for that event. For Category I enrollment after retirement or loss of spousal dependent status, it lists a pension-number record, identity evidence, and proof of the relevant coverage-change date. Eligible notifications can be filed at City Hall or the listed branches, or sent by post with the insured-person notification form and required evidence. A representative normally needs authorization; changes handled through an employer should go to the employer." },
      { title: "Route exemption and student applications separately", description: "Chuo accepts contribution exemption, payment postponement, and Student Special Payment applications at the main Pension Section or Chuo Pension Office, not its branch offices. These applications can also be mailed or filed through My Number Portal. A student application needs a student ID copy or an original enrollment certificate; ask about extra evidence for special exemption circumstances. The ward's electronic overview does not establish that every pension notification has an online form, so check the current form list before filing." },
    ],
