    title: "National Pension in Shinjuku", summary: "Shinjuku takes National Pension enrollment at the ward office's Pension Section or a special branch office, but contribution exemptions and the student system only at the ward office, by post, or online.",
    applicability: "Use Shinjuku's procedures if Shinjuku is your registered municipality and your coverage category calls for a National Pension filing.", responsibleBody: "Shinjuku City", receivingOffice: "Pension Section of the Medical Insurance and Pension Division, fourth floor of the ward office, or a special branch office for enrollment",
    actions: [
      { title: "Enroll after registering or leaving workplace coverage", description: "If you register as a resident at age 20 or later, you enroll at the municipality where you are registered. After leaving a job with employee pension coverage, you become a Category I insured person from the day after you leave, and so does a dependent spouse; file at the Pension Section or a special branch office with your Basic Pension Number Notice or pension handbook and a document showing when you left. Starting a job is handled by the employer. Bring photo identification such as a residence card; a representative needs a letter of authorization. Filing by post or online through Mynaportal is also possible." },
      { title: "Apply for relief at the ward office, by post, or online", description: "Contribution exemptions, postponement for people under 50, and the Student Special Payment System are handled by the Pension Section on the fourth floor, not by special branch offices, and also by post or through Mynaportal. Applications can cover up to two years and one month in the past; one application covers July to the following June (April to March for students). Results come from Japan Pension Service after several months, and payments by account transfer continue until approval. Foreign residents leaving Japan should ask the pension office about the lump-sum withdrawal payment." },
    ],
    sourceIds: ["shinjuku-national-pension-foreign-residents","shinjuku-national-pension-procedures","shinjuku-national-pension-relief","shinjuku-national-pension-identification"], sourceFormatNote: "Shinjuku's pension pages are in Japanese. This English summary is Nihonest guidance, not an official translation.",
